hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19239","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Affan said in his hadith: Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Malik ibn Amr al-Qushayri who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever frees a Muslim neck, it is his ransom from the Fire. Affan said: In place of each bone of the bones of its freer with a bone of his bones. Whoever reaches one of his parents then is not forgiven, Allah has cast him far. Whoever takes an orphan from between two Muslim parents, Affan said: To his food and drink until Allah enriches him, Paradise is assured for him."
